npm i 
    react ->  manage external libraries, automate build processes, and share reusable 
        code components efficiently across projects

    react-dom -> serves as the glue between React's core component logic and the 
        browser's Document Object Model (DOM).

    tailwindcss -> It lets you register Tailwind directly into your local build pipeline

    tailwindcss/vite -> compiles your CSS utility classes natively during development and production builds

    react-router-dom -> for implementing client-side routing in React web applications. 
        It allows you to build single-page applications (SPAs) with multiple views, 
        navigating between pages seamlessly without full browser reloads
    
    react-hot-toast ->  is a lightweight, highly customizable, 
        and open-source notification library for React applications. 
        It weighs under 5kb and provides smooth, animated push-style alerts 
        (toasts) out of the box

    lucide-react ->icon library that provides clean, consistent,
        and customizable SVG icons as React components
    
    luxon (due to no maintainance of moment) -> modern JavaScript library 
        designed for working with dates and times.

    axios -> promise-based JavaScript HTTP client used in browsers and Node.js

    @codesandbox/sandpack-react -> to embed live, interactive code editors and 
        previews directly into your React applications. ( live editing of ai generated code )
    
    file-saver -> solution for saving files on the client-side 
        (to add the codes to the sandbox as codes are saved in the sandbox)

    jszip ->  lets you create, read, and edit ZIP files directly in your browser or Node.js ( to export the code )

    lodash.debounce -> implement an auto-save feature in codesandbox using the lodash.debounce 
        package by delaying your save function until the user stops typing for a set time.

